{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789298485,"nonce":"BMHk2nbojK6vYzABK3gIaVsKTqo=","title":"Register a host module into a decoded program before it runs","message":"The host (caribou) knows, before a program runs, the classes another\nlanguage exposes to Haxe: names, fields, methods with HashLink-typed\nsignatures, and for each method a C entry point that performs the call.\nLet it register those into the decoded program, so a Haxe call into one\nis an ordinary call in ash's own tables and IR, with no library to\nresolve and no dlopen.\n\nRegistration extends the DecodedBytecode after decode and before the\ninterpreter is built, or through an entry the interpreter exposes before\nexecute_entrypoint:\n- types: one HOBJ HLTypeObj per class (name, fields, protos, the $Class\n  companion for statics) appended to `types`; the layout oracle and\n  hlp_get_obj_rt treat it like any decoded class.\n- functions: each method becomes an entry in the shared findex numbering\n  as an HLNative whose lib is the host's tag and whose target the host\n  supplies as a function pointer plus hl_type_fun signature (a typed C\n  call, which every tier already emits and marshals), or, where the host\n  prefers, as a function whose AIR body it hands in (air::v2::Function),\n  installed into the SSA cache for that findex. Natives are the smaller\n  step and give identical behaviour at every tier; AIR bodies allow the\n  tiers to inline and specialise later.\n- the dense per-findex tables (functions_ptrs, beads, entries, sigs,\n  native caches) are sized from the extended counts.\n- the type table's global for the class object is created the way\n  hlp_type_set_global does for decoded classes, so `new` and statics\n  resolve.\n\nThe Haxe side then compiles against a class the build macro emits with\nthe same name, whose methods are @:hlNative(\"\u003chost tag\u003e\", \"\u003csymbol\u003e\")\nwith the signatures the registration promises; at load, ash matches each\ndeclared native to the registered entry by (lib, name) and never looks\nfor a library on disk. If the program's declaration and the registration\ndisagree in signature, loading fails with a diagnostic naming both.\n\nDefault: nothing registered, ash unchanged.","files":null}]}